fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, "STAGE27A_SELLER_ONBOARDING_GUIDE.md"), `# SokoYetu Stage 27A: Seller Onboarding and Verification Guide

Stage 27A defines the seller onboarding workflow for soft launch.

This stage does not change checkout, M-PESA, DNS, email forwarding, database schema, product import or LiveKit logic.

## Seller onboarding flow

\`\`\`text
Seller applies
→ Admin checks identity/contact details
→ Admin checks business/product category
→ Admin checks fulfilment ability
→ Admin approves, rejects, requests more information or suspends
\`\`\`

## Seller statuses

Use these operational statuses:

\`\`\`text
Application Received
Documents Requested
Under Review
Approved
Rejected
Suspended
\`\`\`

## Minimum seller information

\`\`\`text
Seller name
Business name
Phone number
Email address
Location
Product categories
Delivery/pickup ability
Sample product photos
Return/refund approach
\`\`\`

## Soft launch rule

During soft launch, sellers should not publish products without admin review. Admin should verify seller details and product reliability before promotion.
`);

fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, "STAGE27A_SELLER_VERIFICATION_CHECKLIST.md"), `# SokoYetu Stage 27A: Seller Verification Checklist

Use this checklist before approving a seller.

## Identity and contact

- [ ] Seller name recorded.
- [ ] Business name recorded.
- [ ] Phone number confirmed.
- [ ] Email address confirmed.
- [ ] Location recorded.
- [ ] Main contact person identified.

## Product and category

- [ ] Product categories are allowed.
- [ ] Product descriptions are clear.
- [ ] Product images are real or supplier-approved.
- [ ] Prices are realistic.
- [ ] Stock levels are confirmed.
- [ ] Warranty or return expectations are clear where relevant.

## Risk checks

- [ ] No counterfeit wording.
- [ ] No illegal or restricted product.
- [ ] No misleading claims.
- [ ] No suspicious payment request outside SokoYetu.
- [ ] No pressure to bypass admin review.

## Fulfilment

- [ ] Seller can prepare item after paid order.
- [ ] Seller can support pickup, rider collection or delivery.
- [ ] Seller understands customer communication process.
- [ ] Seller agrees to admin order confirmation during soft launch.

## Decision

- [ ] Approved.
- [ ] More information requested.
- [ ] Rejected.
- [ ] Suspended.
`);

